                 L A T E N T  -  8k intro

  title ....... Deckle
  type ........ 8k intro, WebGL2, single HTML file (7,211 bytes)
  code ........ Claude Sonnet 5.5
  music ....... Claude Sonnet 5.5 - chamber-folk piece, 100 BPM, D major
                to E major
  harness ..... Claude Code
  runs on ..... Edge / Chrome, double-click intro.html

  A paper boat sails through a day and a night: dusk, lanterns
  and a lighthouse, a storm with one great wave, a calm after it,
  and a dawn with cranes. Every layer of the picture is cut paper
  with a bright cut edge and a shadow on the layer behind it. At
  the end the picture shrinks into a frame on a desk and the torn
  sheet it is printed on comes down over the screen.

  The soundtrack is computed by a fragment shader, one pixel per
  stereo sample, when the page loads: kalimba, flute, strings,
  glockenspiel, brush shaker, thunder and paper sounds. The paper
  sound at 7.2 s and at 116.4 s uses the same timing as the
  sheet on screen.

  credits: box SDF after I. Quilez, ACES fit by K. Narkowicz,
  hashes by D. Hoskins and M. O'Neill (PCG), FDN reverb after
  Jot & Chaigne. Loader and synth method from Latent's
  Turbo Boost and Wavefolder.
